   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>16.3 (15.8 - 16.9)</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/79/79bc2285bd0564390e0d.png\" /></p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "type": "NAT",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>The number of encirclements N of the origin for the given figure is _____</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4a/4ab2aa7a7fb5e145243f.png\" /></p>",
   "options": [],
   "answer": null,
   "natRange": [
    3,
    3
   ],
   "answerText": "3",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>3 (3 - 3)</p>\n\n<p>Beginning at the point &alpha;, we rotate a radial line from the origin to the contour in the direction of arrows. Three counter clockwise rotation of 360&deg; results in the radial line returning to the point &alpha;. Hence, <em>N</em> = 3.</p>"
  },
